# the ELF model to and from the neutral object
#
# to_neutral reads a relocatable ELF model into a neutral object through the
# tables below and the relocation set of the file's architecture. what the
# neutral model has no field for travels in the object's facts, keyed by ELF,
# so nothing a file states is dropped and the conversion back gives the same
# file contents. from_neutral builds the ELF model of a neutral object, string
# tables included, for the writer to lay out.
#
# the neutral symbols are the symbol table's entries, in order, the null
# symbol first, so a relocation names the symbol it names in the file and a
# table that points into the symbol table stays valid. sections that only
# structure the file, the string tables, the symbol table, the relocation
# sections and the groups, have no neutral section: the relocations and
# groups they hold are the object's own. the GNU property note is a neutral
# section with no bytes of its own, so a symbol defined in it has its place,
# and its properties are the object's traits and facts, which from_neutral
# writes into it. the build attributes section of the architecture's vendor
# is the same, when it has the one shape mink reads, and is otherwise held as
# its bytes.

